{
 "question": "Evidence 62 found one frame of one track that this decoder would not decode and that FFmpeg and Dolby's decoder decode: its checksums are right, and a group of three 3-level mantissas in it has the code 27, which the standard gives no meaning. Five quantisers have such codes, seventeen in all. What does Dolby's decoder make of each, and does this decoder, made to do the same, decode the track as Dolby's does?",
 "method": "A frame of a clean stream of AC-3 is taken, and a group or a code of each of the five quantisers in its middle is written over with each of the codes above its range in turn, the checksums made right again (`oadec repair`); the frame is as long in bits as it was, so everything else in it reads as before. A throwaway build of this decoder reads such a code with the mantissas a variable names. A decode is linear in a mantissa, so a decode of a clip around the frame with nothing in the mantissas of the code and one with 1 in each of them in turn give every other, and the values that bring the frame nearest to what Dolby's decoder wrote, by least squares over the samples the frame reaches, are the values Dolby's decoder gave them; how near the frame then is says whether values are all there is to it. FFmpeg's decode is solved for the same way. The frame of the library is solved for the same way. Then the decoder made to read a code above its range as the highest of the range decodes the whole track, and the decode is held frame by frame to FFmpeg's and to Dolby's, as in evidence 62. The mutations of the change are run against the tests, and the binary before the change and after it are run over the corpus with every report and every delivery compared. No name of a file is kept in what is written here.",
 "commands": [
  "oadec repair -o <clip> <clip with a code written over>",
  "OADEC_EXP_VALS=<a>,<b>,<c> <throwaway oadec> decode --format pcm -o <ours.pcm> <clip>",
  "gst-launch-1.0 filesrc location=<clip> ! dlbac3parse ! dlbac3dec drc-suppress=true out-ch-config=0 ! audio/x-raw,format=F32LE ! filesink location=<dolby.f32>",
  "ffmpeg -drc_scale 0 -f ac3 -i <clip> -f f32le -c:a pcm_f32le <ffmpeg.f32>",
  "oadec verify --json --max-per-rule 4000 <kept track>; oadec decode --format wav -o <ours.wav> <kept track>",
  "python tools/mutants.py --only <the nine mutations of the change>",
  "python tools/old_new.py --old <before> --new <after> --decode-all <corpus>"
 ],
